WEBVTT

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:13.240
In the heart of Africa, a young family is heading for an epic adventure.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:29.680
They are moving with their three children to a remote Kenyan wilderness.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:34.680
Mum Saba is here to run a safari camp.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.520
Welcome!

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:38.560
While dad Frank is helping to protect elephants.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:40.600
Collar's almost on.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:42.600
Now the scary bit.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:48.920
But raising a family and running a business in the bush is going to be a massive challenge.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:51.280
There are monkeys in the kitchen...

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:53.160
Oh, you monkeys, I'm going to kill you!

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:55.960
..Floods threatening the camp...

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:56.840
It's looking like it's going to be a mega storm.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:57.680
..Medical emergencies...

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:59.920
It's bad and it needs urgent action.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:00.520
..And wildlife in need of help.

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:04.480
My heart really is in my mouth.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:06.880
It's going to be a huge gamble.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:11.680
Will the business survive Saba's first season in charge?

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:21.840
This time, the tourist season has started and camp is full.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:25.880
But Saba is pulled away to try to help an injured crocodile...

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:26.720
Can you pull it out?

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:28.520
Pull it out, Ronno?

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:35.840
..And the camp team races to find a four-year-old child missing in the bush.

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:36.840
Lions are all over the place.

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:38.720
It's a very, very serious situation.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:55.040
It's the second week of the season at Elephant Watch, and guests are on their way.

00:01:54.160 --> 00:02:01.440
Saba has only just taken over managing the camp, but she's never run a business before.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:09.000
Just rushing around a bit like a chicken with my head cut off in the, sort of, last five minutes before everybody arrives...

00:02:08.199 --> 00:02:16.840
..and then I have to wipe the sweat off my face and put on a smile and say, "Hello, everybody, welcome to Elephant Watch."

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:24.760
Today, Saba has two groups of guests arriving.

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:29.160
The camp's 12 beds will be full for the first time.

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:32.680
It's their biggest test yet.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:43.760
People come here from all over the world and have high expectations.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:54.160
The business relies on word of mouth, so Saba and the team must make sure every guest has the experience of a lifetime.

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:56.640
So welcome, everybody.

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:57.920
Come into the mess tent.

00:02:57.160 --> 00:03:00.640
We'll bring all your bags in.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:07.160
This is a new adventure for the whole family.

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:14.320
Husband Frank is taking over operations at Save The Elephants, the family's conservation charity.

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:16.960
But this morning, he's on breakfast duty.

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:22.960
Selkie is five, and twins Mayian and Luna are nearly three.

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:29.480
We try and always have breakfast outside and that means they can make more of a mess, like this one's very good at.

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.400
A real pro mess-maker.

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:31.960
This is life how it should be, I think.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:35.760
Saba grew up exactly like this.

00:03:34.840 --> 00:03:38.640
Definitely very different from how I grew up.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:42.880
Moving here is a big gamble.

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:46.440
The camp doubles as a home and a business.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:48.000
They can only stay in Samburu if Saba can make the camp pay its way.

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:58.080
And the local Samburu community is depending on her, too.

00:03:57.120 --> 00:04:05.320
30 staff and their families rely on Elephant Watch for their livelihood.

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:12.600
Behind the scenes, there's a lot of work to do to keep the business running smoothly, but this morning there's a hitch.

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:22.320
We're absolutely full of people, and they've all just arrived, but, erm...sod's law, we've got a plumbing problem.

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:27.520
The kitchen drain is blocked.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:40.720
I think what's happened over the years is that the pipe got completely clogged up with old teabags and bones and, I mean, I don't know what was going down that sink.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:46.440
And, of course, it has to happen on the day that we're absolutely packed with guests.

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:52.360
Guests pay a lot of money to come here.

00:04:51.400 --> 00:04:58.240
Saba and the team must get it fixed before the smell drifts to the breakfast table.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:12.560
Peter's come up with a rather ingenious solution - just get a whole lot of big rocks, which will help with the drainage, and then we'll cover it with plastic and wood and sand, so I think this is going to be a quick solution for now.

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:22.400
The camp's reputation depends on happy guests, so every aspect of their stay must be perfect.

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:28.960
Wildlife guide Litus is preparing the picnic for today's game drive.

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:35.160
It's his job to give these guests a memorable experience.

00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:36.440
Hope you guys had a good breakfast.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:40.360
We had a delicious breakfast.

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:44.880
But this is what the guests really come to see.

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:50.080
These elephants are unusually trusting of humans.

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:54.560
Litus grew up here and knows them well.

00:05:54.400 --> 00:06:02.480
The Samburu people have lived in Northern Kenya for centuries.

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:05.320
This vast wilderness is their home.

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:15.440
Samburu warriors still live and dress as they have for hundreds of years.

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:24.960
They are nomadic herdsmen and rely on their livestock for their food and income.

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:31.080
But survival in this harsh landscape depends on close-knit communities.

00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:40.840
Tourism now provides a secondary income for the Samburu people, and many warriors work at Saba's safari camp.

00:06:39.880 --> 00:06:44.560
Today, they've brought some alarming news.

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:48.560
A four-year-old Samburu girl is lost in the bush.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:50.320
The child disappeared at ten o'clock yesterday morning.

00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:50.640
It's a little girl.

00:06:49.680 --> 00:07:01.160
She's the same age as Selkie, a bit younger, and, er, she was heading back to her manyatta to go and get water, left another group of children, and she hasn't been seen since.

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:10.840
It's on the other side of the river, unfortunately, so I can't get a car across, but I think they need to track her on foot, so the sooner we get everyone out there, the better.

00:07:10.240 --> 00:07:14.760
OK, everybody, listen.

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:15.040
Good luck.

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:15.360
Please, good luck.

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:21.080
The camp team know the area intimately.

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:26.480
They started herding livestock here at an early age.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:29.640
You know, if anyone's going to find her, it's these guys.

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:32.360
Bernard's there, Mporian's there.

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:32.840
I know her entire village is out looking for her.

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:44.320
Everybody in camp has gone and they've probably called in some other villages as well, so they'll just be, you know, going back and forth until they find her tracks and then they can home in.

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:48.040
These guys, these nomads, are some of the best trackers in the business.

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:51.880
Camp guide Bernard knows how dangerous it can be in the bush.

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:55.680
Everybody is worried, because there are a lot of animals.

00:07:54.720 --> 00:08:10.640
Lions are all over the place, elephants as well, and you can imagine a tiny, little baby doesn't even know how to protect itself or hide, so it's a very, very serious situation.

00:08:11.120 --> 00:08:22.280
Samburu children are taught how to survive outdoors from the moment they are born, but they never stay out after dark.

00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:28.080
This is when nocturnal predators hunt.

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:31.440
Even elephants can be dangerous.

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:41.039
They can only hope that the little girl has found a safe place to hide overnight.

00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:48.880
Out in the reserve, camp guide Litus is unaware of the situation.

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:56.480
He's showing guests wildlife from the safety of their vehicle.

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:59.200
Just incredible.

00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:00.520
That is amazing.

00:09:00.400 --> 00:09:04.680
It is a lifetime...

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:06.320
Once in a lifetime experience.

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:08.880
One I'd like to do a lot more of.

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:12.920
I didn't expect that we'd be this close.

00:09:12.040 --> 00:09:15.840
I thought they'd be off across the river.

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:18.080
Oh, they're beautiful.

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:27.600
They seem calm, but you can never take wild animals for granted.

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:33.440
This young bull is letting them know not to come any closer.

00:09:44.360 --> 00:09:47.440
That's how they what?

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:54.960
He wanted to kill us?

00:09:54.160 --> 00:10:01.640
This adolescent male is just flexing his muscles, but if he encountered people this close on foot, it would be a different matter.

00:10:02.840 --> 00:10:09.760
The lost girl has now been missing for 24 hours.

00:10:08.800 --> 00:10:14.560
There's no sign of her, but one of the warriors spots a possible clue.

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:20.960
You look at every inch of the ground where you think the tracks are.

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:28.440
It may be, you know, the baby was playing along, and maybe picked up the rock or maybe knocked the rock off the ground.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:28.960
It's highly possible that it's the baby who knocked that rock off.

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:40.280
They're on the right trail, but the search party is stopped in its tracks.

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:44.560
An adult bull elephant is blocking the way.

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:52.000
Very, very dangerous, but as long as you're behind a big tree, you're safe.

00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:54.200
That is why these guys are right behind this big branch.

00:10:53.320 --> 00:10:57.040
That way, the elephant cannot pick you out.

00:10:56.120 --> 00:10:57.600
Fortunately, the trackers are downwind of the elephant.

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:05.240
He hasn't noticed them, so they sneak by undetected.

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:11.320
With dangerous animals in the area, the worst-case scenarios are running through Bernard's mind.

00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:16.480
Some of these predators, they rely on what they can find.

00:11:16.160 --> 00:11:23.800
Carcasses or human beings, and they can easily attack.

00:11:22.920 --> 00:11:26.000
Even adults, not just a baby.

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:32.440
To make matters worse, this landscape provides perfect cover for predators.

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:35.240
These are a very good hideout for a lot of animals.

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:43.360
If a leopard kills a goat or a lion, they will tuck it inside these thick, thick bushes and there is no way you can see it.

00:11:42.480 --> 00:11:46.360
So, for a baby, that's like nothing.

00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:54.760
To cover more area and increase their chances of finding the four-year-old girl, the search party splits in two.

00:11:53.840 --> 00:11:57.160
I'm so anxious about this little child.

00:11:56.200 --> 00:12:06.800
If it was Selkie and I was the parents, I'd be absolutely beside myself because a four, five-year-old out there on its own, just...

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:08.720
You know, it's exceedingly dangerous.

00:12:07.880 --> 00:12:17.160
You know, it's very dry, she probably hasn't had anything to drink for a long time, and God knows where she is.

00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:20.240
They're fearing the worst.

00:12:19.400 --> 00:12:20.800
Bernard's team gets a call from the other search party.

00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:22.480
Ah, it's been found!

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:34.240
Whoo!

00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:42.800
The baby slept out in the bush and luckily she survived whatever is out there, and they're taking the baby home.

00:12:42.560 --> 00:12:44.800
So that is incredible.

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:56.520
For a four-year-old to sleep out in the bush in the wild, and to be alive in the morning, that is the most amazing news I've heard in a long time.

00:12:55.880 --> 00:13:12.720
According to Samburu tradition, the finder of the baby will get a cow from the baby's family, and they will slaughter a few goats today as a sign of celebration.

00:13:11.920 --> 00:13:17.120
So it will be a very, very happy party time this evening in that specific village.

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:21.200
But the homecoming celebration won't begin until much later this evening.

00:13:20.240 --> 00:13:25.200
Bernard and the team return to give Saba the good news.

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:26.880
We are so happy.

00:13:26.120 --> 00:13:27.600
Oh, my God.

00:13:26.720 --> 00:13:29.400
The baby was found by the other search party.

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:31.960
Oh, well done.

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:39.040
I was just thinking of what it would be like if Selkie or the twins were out there, as a mother.

00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:40.040
I'm so happy.

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:42.320
Just marvellous news.

00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:42.840
I'm so pleased.

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:44.200
I was so worried.

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:45.000
Yeah.

00:13:44.160 --> 00:13:45.320
Good.

00:13:44.360 --> 00:13:47.960
That's really good news.

00:13:47.000 --> 00:13:49.440
That's made my day.

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:56.200
With the lost child safe, the camp team can prepare for the guests' lunch.

00:13:56.320 --> 00:14:04.960
Maintenance man Peter is putting the finishing touches to the drain, much to the relief of the kitchen staff.

00:14:04.200 --> 00:14:10.480
The guests return from their morning safari none the wiser.

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:16.680
Normally, Saba would be there to greet them, but there's been another emergency.

00:14:15.800 --> 00:14:21.520
This time it's an animal in trouble, and she's on her way to help.

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:28.400
I just got a radio call at the research camp, there's been a...

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:37.400
There's a crocodile that's appeared in front of one of the lodges with a, looks like a spear shaft going through its back and stomach.

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:44.680
There are eight different lodges along the banks of the river in the reserve.

00:14:44.120 --> 00:14:49.400
It's a small community and everyone relies on each other when there's a problem.

00:14:48.680 --> 00:15:00.760
When I woke up this morning, the last thing in the world I thought I'd be doing would be assisting in the treatment of a crocodile, but anything can happen in Samburu.

00:14:59.840 --> 00:15:01.840
Anything at all.

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:04.520
You just never know what's round the corner.

00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:07.280
Here we are, Samburu Lodge.

00:15:06.440 --> 00:15:12.960
The crocodile was speared by a herder protecting his livestock two days ago.

00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:21.120
If they leave it any longer, the wound will become infected and the crocodile could die.

00:15:20.280 --> 00:15:24.040
The Kenya Wildlife Service has been called.

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:28.560
Saba's colleague, David Daballen, is also helping.

00:15:27.680 --> 00:15:30.600
He has a net to try to catch the injured crocodile.

00:15:29.720 --> 00:15:40.120
Last few days, there's been, either the vet has gone for some work or the crocodile has been hiding, but right now we just have everything on site, so this is our mission right now.

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:52.360
15 feet long and weighing over 900lbs, the Nile crocodile has one of the most powerful bites on the planet.

00:15:52.480 --> 00:16:01.280
But as the mission begins, the wounded croc heads for the river.

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:05.200
The croc has just disappeared into the water or into the river, so...

00:16:04.360 --> 00:16:07.720
It's so frustrating.

00:16:07.880 --> 00:16:15.040
I mean, like, how does he know that he has to get in now, just as we came in?

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:16.440
But, anyway, we'll wait.

00:16:15.680 --> 00:16:16.880
We'll be patient.

00:16:16.040 --> 00:16:19.720
You know, this crocodile's very frightened of people, so...

00:16:18.840 --> 00:16:29.760
Obviously cos it's badly wounded, so the difficulty is how they juggle between keeping the other crocodiles away and luring it up here and then getting it caught in the net.

00:16:29.080 --> 00:16:40.160
Cos if they tranquilize it, they can't let it go into the river, because then it'll drown.

00:16:39.800 --> 00:16:42.920
The injured crocodile is not playing ball.

00:16:42.400 --> 00:16:48.640
All Saba and the rescue team can do is wait.

00:17:01.920 --> 00:17:10.800
Keeping the camp running smoothly is one thing, but the reason guests come here is for the safaris.

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:14.720
They are the lifeblood of Saba's business.

00:17:15.240 --> 00:17:22.359
It's up to wildlife guide Bernard to try to find animals for the guests.

00:17:21.400 --> 00:17:23.800
You can never plan anything out here.

00:17:22.839 --> 00:17:36.480
You just go out and things happen and sometimes things don't happen, and that is what makes it even interesting, but every day when I go out, I'm hoping to find lovely elephants.

00:17:35.640 --> 00:17:43.080
Not just because I want to show the elephants to the guests, but also because I want to see them myself and that makes it even more special.

00:17:44.240 --> 00:17:53.400
Bernard grew up in the bush.

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:58.640
His survival depended on being able to spot wildlife.

00:17:58.600 --> 00:18:02.800
Oh, leopard!

00:18:04.040 --> 00:18:07.440
We've got leopards here.

00:18:09.920 --> 00:18:11.320
Right there, right there.

00:18:11.240 --> 00:18:13.240
Oh, my God!

00:18:12.640 --> 00:18:14.240
Oh, my goodness.

00:18:13.440 --> 00:18:16.520
So beautiful.

00:18:18.520 --> 00:18:26.560
Leopards are mostly nocturnal.

00:18:25.840 --> 00:18:28.000
To see one in the middle of the day is rare.

00:18:28.200 --> 00:18:32.000
But people come to Samburu for one animal in particular.

00:18:31.080 --> 00:18:32.840
Oh, elephant!

00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:34.120
Elephant!

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:41.960
(She's so human-like. )

00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:47.720
(It looks like Dumbo from the movie. )

00:18:46.920 --> 00:18:50.920
(It's coming towards us. )

00:18:52.120 --> 00:19:00.360
Wild elephants don't get any closer than this.

00:19:02.200 --> 00:19:04.920
(He's not too sure about it. )

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:07.280
(That's why he puts his trunk back, he's not sure about it. )

00:19:09.840 --> 00:19:11.640
You're OK, don't move.

00:19:12.000 --> 00:19:13.680
She's fine, she's not going to do anything.

00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:16.520
(You can talk to her, slowly. )

00:19:16.120 --> 00:19:17.280
(Yeah, you can talk to her. )

00:19:17.240 --> 00:19:18.360
Can I touch her?

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:19.120
(No, don't touch her. )

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:21.320
So beautiful.

00:19:35.960 --> 00:19:37.320
That was so special.

00:19:36.640 --> 00:19:43.680
For her to trust you like that, you know, that, erm... intimacy is amazing.

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:51.280
How did you like that?

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:54.760
That was incredible!

00:19:56.080 --> 00:20:07.240
Three miles upriver, Saba and the rescue team have a plan to catch the injured crocodile.

00:20:06.480 --> 00:20:14.280
Once they've got this net properly set up, we're going to hold it up from this side.

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:17.440
They're going to lure the crocodile up with some meat.

00:20:16.600 --> 00:20:22.360
I don't quite know how they're going to prevent other crocodiles coming up for it as well, but that remains to be seen.

00:20:23.720 --> 00:20:32.960
Anyway, as soon as it's within this area here, we'll let the net go and then they're going to jump down on either side and, sort of, surround it with the net, and it'll be captured.

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:33.480
Sounds a bit dodgy to me.

00:20:34.480 --> 00:20:38.960
With the net in place, the trap is set.

00:20:38.160 --> 00:20:42.280
But the crocodile is still in the river.

00:20:41.480 --> 00:20:42.960
I can see the crocs are right down there.

00:20:42.120 --> 00:20:47.920
Some of them were in the middle of the river.

00:20:47.840 --> 00:20:49.800
Let's see what happens.

00:20:48.840 --> 00:20:51.000
They only have one chance to get this right.

00:20:50.120 --> 00:20:56.280
We're going to do a practice run, and I'm going to be the crocodile.

00:20:55.320 --> 00:20:56.880
See how it goes.

00:21:06.800 --> 00:21:08.920
Well, the net's in place.

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:11.960
Everything's ready.

00:21:13.280 --> 00:21:17.960
It's just a matter of getting the crocodile out of the water.

00:21:17.320 --> 00:21:25.080
That may not happen until this evening, it depends on how nervous it is around people and this new arrangement.

00:21:24.240 --> 00:21:34.440
There's a lot of people who've come out, I mean this is a little bit more exciting than working in the kitchen at the back for most of the staff in the lodge.

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:44.280
Crocodiles can't resist fresh meat, and it's soon lured up the bank.

00:21:44.000 --> 00:21:45.800
We've only got once chance at this, so it has to work.

00:21:47.560 --> 00:21:50.840
Let's just hope it's successful.

00:21:52.280 --> 00:21:58.560
The plan's working, but there's a problem.

00:21:57.760 --> 00:22:01.160
They've got more crocodiles than they bargained for.

00:22:01.480 --> 00:22:08.000
Back in camp, the guests are settling in for the evening.

00:22:13.680 --> 00:22:17.920
That was amazing.

00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:25.000
Bernard's given them a safari experience they'll never forget.

00:22:24.280 --> 00:22:32.600
His work is done, but the day isn't over yet.

00:22:36.600 --> 00:22:48.600
Bernard and the other warriors from this morning's search party are going to meet the lost girl and share the family's celebrations.

00:22:48.640 --> 00:22:53.040
The little girl was found and everybody is very jovial.

00:22:52.120 --> 00:22:56.920
We're actually getting into the manyatta where her family lives.

00:22:56.080 --> 00:23:11.520
The elders are dancing and the warriors, so it's going to be a very emotional moment, especially for the parents.

00:23:10.600 --> 00:23:36.800
The family is putting on a feast to celebrate the little girl's safe return.

00:23:36.000 --> 00:23:46.200
But first, the village elders perform an ancient cleansing ritual with herbs and water.

00:23:45.400 --> 00:23:48.560
Everybody here must be tough.

00:23:47.600 --> 00:23:51.120
If you're not tough, you're not going to survive.

00:23:50.240 --> 00:23:51.520
And it starts from a tiny age.

00:23:50.720 --> 00:24:01.320
When they become a bit older, like ten years, they're fully capable of taking care of themselves and their livestock, because they go out in the field.

00:24:00.720 --> 00:24:06.840
They've learnt all the skills that are needed to be able to survive in this kind of environment.

00:24:07.520 --> 00:24:11.800
The ceremony is over.

00:24:10.960 --> 00:24:16.400
The child has been welcomed home.

00:24:20.720 --> 00:24:24.400
Now the party can begin.

00:24:36.640 --> 00:24:48.080
Back with the wounded crocodile, Saba and the team can't celebrate yet.

00:24:47.280 --> 00:24:48.560
There's a toothy complication.

00:24:47.760 --> 00:24:53.320
The injured crocodile is on the bank, but it's surrounded by other crocs drawn in by the meat.

00:24:52.480 --> 00:25:08.440
The nine crocodiles that have been here this afternoon, we have to lure them, somehow, off to the left and at the same time lure the wounded crocodile far over to the right, so that we can separate them and drop the net.

00:25:07.760 --> 00:25:12.760
Yeah, that's definitely him, that's the one.

00:25:16.960 --> 00:25:18.480
I can see the spear shaft.

00:25:17.720 --> 00:25:21.920
Oh, man.

00:25:21.480 --> 00:25:30.480
He's looking very lethargic and not really all that interested in the meat, unlike the other crocodiles.

00:25:29.920 --> 00:25:33.960
I would imagine that he's suffering a lot.

00:25:33.160 --> 00:25:48.120
You know, these poor, old crocodiles, no-one really has much love for a crocodile, but they're an incredibly important part of this ecosystem, and keeping it all whole and diverse and healthy.

00:25:47.720 --> 00:25:51.560
The rescue team is running out of time.

00:25:50.600 --> 00:25:54.240
This is the last desperate attempt to get this finished tonight.

00:25:53.600 --> 00:25:54.920
OK, we're very close now.

00:25:54.160 --> 00:25:56.920
A few more like that.

00:25:56.000 --> 00:25:58.800
Further away.

00:25:58.680 --> 00:25:59.880
Wait.

00:26:04.560 --> 00:26:05.760
Wait.

00:26:05.280 --> 00:26:06.920
Yep, yep.

00:26:11.760 --> 00:26:18.240
The net's down, but the crocodile is only partially snared.

00:26:17.280 --> 00:26:19.880
Can you get it under its feet?

00:26:19.080 --> 00:26:21.960
Under that foot?

00:26:24.520 --> 00:26:32.640
Yeah, I mean, it's not a good position right now.

00:26:32.880 --> 00:26:39.000
It's actually wiggling its way out and going backwards and it's hanging right over the bank.

00:26:38.280 --> 00:26:43.560
If the crocodile falls into the river wrapped in the net, it will drown.

00:26:43.320 --> 00:26:49.640
The men are being dragged towards the water.

00:26:50.680 --> 00:26:53.960
You just don't understand how strong these creatures are.

00:26:53.240 --> 00:27:02.440
They started with four men trying to close the net around it, and ended up with about 30, all of whom were being pulled down towards the river by the crocodile.

00:27:03.160 --> 00:27:06.720
They need to act quickly to remove the spear.

00:27:08.320 --> 00:27:09.440
Can you pull it out?

00:27:08.640 --> 00:27:11.360
Pull it out.

00:27:10.600 --> 00:27:12.000
So, this is what was inside of him.

00:27:11.240 --> 00:27:14.520
I mean, it's...

00:27:15.320 --> 00:27:17.160
Look how he's bent that metal, and that was deep inside his gut.

00:27:17.400 --> 00:27:29.200
But there's no sign of infection to my unpractised eye, and now he's had a big dose of antibiotics, so let's just hope this does the trick.

00:27:30.560 --> 00:27:33.920
With the spearhead removed, the crocodile can be released.

00:27:33.240 --> 00:27:35.240
But there's a snag.

00:27:38.240 --> 00:27:39.480
He says it's almost completely out of the net.

00:27:38.720 --> 00:27:46.040
It's just there's one rope that's kind of stuck around the tail.

00:27:45.440 --> 00:27:51.600
With one final tug on the rope, the crocodile is free.

00:27:51.080 --> 00:27:56.520
Today, Saba and the camp team have been put to the test.

00:27:55.880 --> 00:28:05.720
With help from their friends, they've saved a crocodile, rescued a child, and kept the family business on track.

00:28:06.600 --> 00:28:09.680
Just another day in Samburu!

00:28:08.840 --> 00:28:13.320
Next time... the rainy season arrives in Samburu.

00:28:12.360 --> 00:28:15.360
Looking like it's going to be a megastorm.

00:28:14.600 --> 00:28:16.160
The camp is under threat.

00:28:15.400 --> 00:28:18.840
Both people and animals are struggling.

00:28:17.960 --> 00:28:22.280
Poor Cheri.

00:28:21.320 --> 00:28:28.760
I've known her for such a long time, and she has something terribly, terribly wrong.

00:28:27.840 --> 00:28:30.560
The only thing we can do, and it's a very difficult decision, is maybe try to rescue the calf.

00:28:29.600 --> 00:28:30.760
Hello, I'm Charlie Brooker.

00:28:29.800 --> 00:28:30.920
Please join me for 2015 Wipe, looking back at a year containing pig-gate, Clarkson-gate, Fifa-gate, Hatton Garden-gate, white and gold or blue and black, the election, Corbynmania, Poldark, Isis, the refugee crisis, Ashley Madison, Cecil the lion, Syria, Dave's epic strut and Donald Trump, amongst other things.

00:28:30.160 --> 00:28:32.000
That's 2015 Wipe, Wednesday 30th December, 9pm, BBC Two.

00:28:31.040 --> 00:28:32.440
BBC Two tells the story...

00:28:31.480 --> 00:28:32.640
Squad, 'shun!

00:28:31.720 --> 00:28:33.040
..Of a courageous campaign...

00:28:32.360 --> 00:28:33.600
Don't panic, Mr Perry!

00:28:32.640 --> 00:28:33.800
..And a major result...

00:28:32.920 --> 00:28:34.040
I did like that voice of yours.

00:29:24.640 --> 00:29:25.720
Oh, did you, Mr Mainwaring?

00:29:24.880 --> 00:29:25.960
..Against impossible odds.

00:29:45.120 --> 00:29:46.240
Be a battle to get this through.

00:29:53.520 --> 00:29:54.640
We're Doomed!

00:29:54.000 --> 00:29:55.440
The Dad's Army Story.

00:29:54.680 --> 00:29:55.920
Reporting for duty...

00:29:54.960 --> 00:29:57.120
Meet the lizard that fakes its own death.

